   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "וְזוֹקֵק לְיִבּוּם. דִּכְתִיב: ״כִּי יֵשְׁבוּ אַחִים יַחְדָּו״ — אַחִים שֶׁהָיָה לָהֶם יְשִׁיבָה אַחַת בָּעוֹלָם.",
   "en": "The mishna also teaches: «And» a one-day-old baby «creates» a levirate bond requiring the widow of his childless brother «to» enter into «levirate marriage» with him. The Gemara explains that this is derived from that «which is written: “If brothers dwell together» and one of them dies, and he has no child, the wife of the dead man shall not be married outside of the family to one not of his kin. Her brother-in-law will have intercourse with her and take her to him to be his wife, and consummate the levirate marriage” (Deuteronomy 25:5). This verse is referring to «brothers who had one dwelling in the world,» i.e., who were alive at the same time, which includes a baby who was born the day his brother died."
  }
 ],
